This architecture provides a complete, production-ready, modular Cloud-Native API Gateway implemented in C# using ASP.NET Core 8.0/9.0. It integrates **YARP (Yet Another Reverse Proxy)** for high-performance routing, **Asymmetric JWT Verification** (RS256) with custom fine-grained scope authorization, and a high-performance **W3C/X-Correlation-ID Distributed Tracing Subsystem**.

```
                           [ Downstream Client ]
                                     │
   ┌─────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┐
   │ API Gateway (ASP.NET Core)      ▼                                 │
   │   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
   │   │ Distributed Tracing Middleware                              │ │
   │   │ - Generates/Extracts Trace IDs & "X-Correlation-ID"         │ │
   │   │ - Sets AsyncLocal/Logger Logging Scopes                     │ │
   │   └─────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘ │
   │                                 ▼                                 │
   │   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
   │   │ Cryptographic Auth & Policy Subsystem                       │ │
   │   │ - Validates RS256 Signatures via JWKS / Ephemeral Public Key│ │
   │   │ - Inspects Scopes (e.g., 'orders.read', 'catalog.write')    │ │
   │   └─────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘ │
   │                                 ▼                                 │
   │   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
   │   │ YARP Routing & Transform Engine                             │ │
   │   │ - Dynamically maps incoming routes to Service Clusters      │ │
   │   │ - Inject Trace/Correlation Headers into outgoing Requests   │ │
   │   └─────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘ │
   └─────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┘
                                     │ (Forwarded Request)
                                     ▼
                      [ Microservice Clusters ]
                  (Catalog Service / Order Service)
```

